1
00:00:00,410 --> 00:00:01,810
(All characters, places,
and organizations are fictional.)

2
00:00:01,810 --> 00:00:03,310
(Children and teens were filmed
under production guidelines.)

3
00:00:05,110 --> 00:00:06,340
Welcome, ma'am.

4
00:00:06,810 --> 00:00:09,310
I do not think we have met before.
Do you have a reservation?

5
00:00:09,680 --> 00:00:13,750
- Are you the manager here?
- Yes, I am Manager Kang Da Mi.

6
00:00:14,190 --> 00:00:16,920
It is a pleasure to meet you.
How may I help...

7
00:00:18,690 --> 00:00:19,690
Da Mi.

8
00:00:22,730 --> 00:00:24,560
What is the meaning of this, ma'am?

9
00:00:24,660 --> 00:00:26,130
(K Department Store)

10
00:00:26,900 --> 00:00:27,900
Pick it up.

11
00:00:28,400 --> 00:00:30,470
- Excuse me?
- Pick it up and see...

12
00:00:30,540 --> 00:00:31,670
for yourself.

13
00:00:35,040 --> 00:00:36,570
You pick it up, ma'am.

14
00:00:37,940 --> 00:00:38,940
What?

15
00:00:39,410 --> 00:00:41,980
You heard me.
I said the person who threw it...

16
00:00:42,110 --> 00:00:44,950
- should pick it up.
- You asked what I meant.

17
00:00:45,620 --> 00:00:48,120
If you are curious, pick it up
and see for yourself.

18
00:00:48,250 --> 00:00:50,190
This is the department store's
VIP boutique.

19
00:00:50,690 --> 00:00:52,260
It is not your personal shoe closet.

20
00:00:52,260 --> 00:00:53,930
When did I say it was my closet?

21
00:00:54,460 --> 00:00:58,460
If those were my shoes,
I wouldn't be making such a fuss.

22
00:00:58,730 --> 00:00:59,760
Those shoes...

23
00:01:00,700 --> 00:01:03,330
You know exactly
whose they are, right?

24
00:01:03,800 --> 00:01:05,870
When I brought our CEO in here,

25
00:01:06,200 --> 00:01:07,470
you were the one
who helped us, right?

26
00:01:08,470 --> 00:01:09,470
Yes.

27
00:01:10,910 --> 00:01:11,980
Our CEO...

28
00:01:12,840 --> 00:01:16,110
is a VVVVIP customer here...

29
00:01:16,580 --> 00:01:18,920
and the CEO of Hwanggeum Apparel.

30
00:01:24,560 --> 00:01:26,190
Do you understand the situation now?

31
00:01:26,690 --> 00:01:27,830
This department store.

32
00:01:28,690 --> 00:01:31,030
Because this lounge
under your management...

33
00:01:31,430 --> 00:01:34,630
did such a shoddy job repairing
our CEO's heel,

34
00:01:35,070 --> 00:01:38,040
she was completely humiliated
at a very important meeting.

35
00:01:38,200 --> 00:01:41,510
Do you realize how much damage
you've caused Hwanggeum Apparel,

36
00:01:41,610 --> 00:01:42,840
yet you dare act so arrogant?

37
00:01:43,410 --> 00:01:45,940
Financial and emotional damages.

38
00:01:46,440 --> 00:01:47,980
How are you going to pay for that?

39
00:01:48,710 --> 00:01:50,580
I can go straight to management
and file a formal complaint...

40
00:01:50,650 --> 00:01:52,280
and have you both...

41
00:01:53,220 --> 00:01:55,520
fired in a heartbeat.

42
00:01:59,290 --> 00:02:00,530
I am so sorry, ma'am.

43
00:02:01,090 --> 00:02:02,690
This is entirely my fault.

44
00:02:03,160 --> 00:02:05,830
Before I returned the shoes
to the CEO,

45
00:02:05,830 --> 00:02:07,600
I should have checked them
thoroughly.

46
00:02:08,270 --> 00:02:10,000
It was my negligence.

47
00:02:10,540 --> 00:02:14,470
I am truly sorry.
Please, I beg you to forgive me...

48
00:02:15,710 --> 00:02:17,310
Kneeling in front of me
won't change anything.

49
00:02:18,040 --> 00:02:21,450
You can't put spilled water
back in the glass.

50
00:02:22,880 --> 00:02:24,620
This is just pathetic and miserable.

51
00:02:25,820 --> 00:02:29,350
What, are you trying to get
some sympathy points...

52
00:02:29,420 --> 00:02:30,420
by doing this?

53
00:02:32,220 --> 00:02:34,190
Min Hee, get up right now.
What are you doing?

54
00:02:34,930 --> 00:02:36,190
Why are you on your knees?

55
00:02:36,900 --> 00:02:38,000
No, Da Mi.

56
00:02:38,500 --> 00:02:41,670
- I am the one who messed up.
- I am your supervisor, Min Hee.

57
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:44,400
Get up. Stand up straight.

58
00:02:47,870 --> 00:02:49,410
Manager Kang Da Mi, was it?

59
00:02:50,640 --> 00:02:53,410
It seems you do not care
if you lose your job.

60
00:02:53,710 --> 00:02:57,050
You do not need to worry
about my job, ma'am.

61
00:02:57,620 --> 00:03:01,050
Regarding the complaint
that you have raised,

62
00:03:01,520 --> 00:03:03,960
it will first be reported
to our department store's...

63
00:03:04,020 --> 00:03:06,090
VIP customer care department
according to procedure.

64
00:03:06,260 --> 00:03:09,190
After that, the CEO will be informed
of the exact details and situation,

65
00:03:09,490 --> 00:03:10,600
and then you will be contacted.

66
00:03:11,300 --> 00:03:15,100
Please return home for today
and wait to hear from us.

67
00:03:16,230 --> 00:03:18,800
We will process this
as quickly as possible, ma'am.

68
00:03:19,640 --> 00:03:20,670
Is that so?

69
00:03:21,670 --> 00:03:24,380
Then my company will also
have to follow procedure.

70
00:03:25,210 --> 00:03:26,380
Let us see how this plays out.

71
00:03:37,520 --> 00:03:39,790
I have definitely seen her before.

72
00:03:40,190 --> 00:03:43,230
Why is that rude little girl
staring at me like that?

73
00:03:43,560 --> 00:03:45,230
Are all rich kids like that?

74
00:03:48,030 --> 00:03:49,130
What is going on, Da Mi?

75
00:03:49,270 --> 00:03:51,670
It is because of that woman
who just left, right?

76
00:03:53,440 --> 00:03:55,340
I live with
an extraordinary Grandma,

77
00:03:55,410 --> 00:03:56,910
so I am very quick to catch on.

78
00:03:57,710 --> 00:04:00,510
That woman who just left
was causing a scene, right?

79
00:04:02,110 --> 00:04:04,920
Looking at your employee's face,
it is pretty obvious.

80
00:04:05,220 --> 00:04:07,290
It is not like that, ma'am.

81
00:04:07,690 --> 00:04:10,520
Oh, come on. Are you going
to keep drawing a line, Da Mi?

82
00:04:10,890 --> 00:04:13,390
Just call me Se Na.

83
00:04:14,390 --> 00:04:17,960
If that is uncomfortable,
how about Ms. Se Na?

84
00:04:18,460 --> 00:04:21,500
Let us compromise on that,
Da Mi. Okay?

85
00:04:23,300 --> 00:04:25,540
Are you looking for anything
specific today?

86
00:04:25,800 --> 00:04:28,710
- I can help you.
- I am not here to buy anything.

87
00:04:30,040 --> 00:04:32,280
Last time, I bought
a bunch of things...

88
00:04:32,380 --> 00:04:33,880
with my brother's card
and returned them.

89
00:04:34,350 --> 00:04:37,680
My brother even came in my place.

90
00:04:39,850 --> 00:04:42,720
I am also thankful that you
found my tablet and returned it.

91
00:04:43,860 --> 00:04:48,290
My soul, blood, sweat,
and tears are all in there.

92
00:04:49,130 --> 00:04:50,460
You know how I feel, right?

93
00:04:51,400 --> 00:04:52,460
I know very well.

94
00:04:53,200 --> 00:04:56,070
You must be thirsty.
Min Hee, please get a drink for her.

95
00:04:56,530 --> 00:04:58,470
Are you offering me a drink?

96
00:04:59,540 --> 00:05:02,810
Then I will have an iced Americano.

97
00:05:03,680 --> 00:05:05,580
Yes, ma'am. Just a moment.

98
00:05:11,920 --> 00:05:12,950
Tell me, Da Mi.

99
00:05:13,720 --> 00:05:17,220
Your expression has been dark,
and so has your employee's.

100
00:05:18,490 --> 00:05:20,630
What exactly happened earlier?

101
00:05:21,490 --> 00:05:23,390
I appreciate your concern.

102
00:05:24,460 --> 00:05:25,760
Ms. Se Na.

103
00:05:28,170 --> 00:05:31,600
I cannot answer that.
Matters regarding our customers...

104
00:05:31,670 --> 00:05:34,770
are strictly between the customer
and the store,

105
00:05:35,210 --> 00:05:37,780
so I absolutely cannot
discuss them with anyone else.

106
00:05:38,940 --> 00:05:41,610
Manager Kang, you are
really professional.

107
00:05:43,310 --> 00:05:47,420
Our souls are definitely connected.

108
00:05:49,190 --> 00:05:51,160
Souls?

109
00:05:55,230 --> 00:05:57,560
It was not me,
but my sister who took it.

110
00:05:57,730 --> 00:05:59,130
She said even the patterns matched.

111
00:05:59,230 --> 00:06:02,430
Didn't you notice? How careless!

112
00:06:04,170 --> 00:06:05,200
Your sister?

113
00:06:07,510 --> 00:06:08,870
Do you not know Cha Se Na?

114
00:06:09,670 --> 00:06:11,140
She took it out in front of you...

115
00:06:11,280 --> 00:06:12,340
and brought back yours by mistake.

116
00:06:13,750 --> 00:06:16,110
Se Na.

117
00:06:16,980 --> 00:06:20,150
Cha Do Yun of Hwanggeum Apparel
is your older brother,

118
00:06:21,350 --> 00:06:25,220
so is designer Jaden Cha
also an older brother to you?

119
00:06:25,520 --> 00:06:28,360
Seung Yun came by here? Already?

120
00:06:29,530 --> 00:06:31,560
Yes, that's right.
He's the eldest among us.

121
00:06:33,060 --> 00:06:35,000
You have two older brothers
too, Se Na.

122
00:06:35,400 --> 00:06:38,370
Why?
Do you have two older brothers too?

123
00:06:39,400 --> 00:06:41,940
Yes, I am the youngest.

124
00:06:42,410 --> 00:06:43,440
Oh my goodness.

125
00:06:44,580 --> 00:06:48,150
See? I told you our souls
are connected.

126
00:06:49,050 --> 00:06:51,180
I am the youngest in my family too.

127
00:06:52,350 --> 00:06:53,520
This is truly amazing.

128
00:06:59,020 --> 00:07:01,760
So you are saying
they complained strongly?

129
00:07:02,130 --> 00:07:03,160
Yes, CEO Jeon.

130
00:07:03,490 --> 00:07:05,460
The department store
has a separate department...

131
00:07:05,560 --> 00:07:08,130
for VIP client management,
so once the report goes up,

132
00:07:08,200 --> 00:07:10,670
they will likely contact you
directly.

133
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:13,970
Did Manager Kang say that herself?

134
00:07:14,240 --> 00:07:15,240
Yes.

135
00:07:17,910 --> 00:07:20,210
Then this matter
is cleanly resolved, right?

136
00:07:21,650 --> 00:07:22,750
Of course, CEO Jeon.

137
00:07:24,880 --> 00:07:25,880
Good.

138
00:07:26,320 --> 00:07:29,050
I am sure you handled it well.

139
00:07:29,620 --> 00:07:31,120
Good work. You may leave.

140
00:07:31,890 --> 00:07:33,320
Also, I have prepared
for the meeting...

141
00:07:33,390 --> 00:07:37,360
with Summit Investment this evening
without any issues, CEO Jeon.

142
00:07:39,730 --> 00:07:43,000
Since we need to secure such a large
investment amount,

143
00:07:44,470 --> 00:07:45,470
I am a bit nervous.

144
00:07:45,770 --> 00:07:48,610
Do you get nervous too, CEO Jeon?

145
00:07:49,270 --> 00:07:50,370
Of course I do.

146
00:07:50,880 --> 00:07:52,210
Am I not human?

147
00:08:00,420 --> 00:08:02,920
Ta-da. Eat up. Please enjoy.

148
00:08:04,590 --> 00:08:05,690
Thank you for the food.

149
00:08:08,890 --> 00:08:10,230
These are stevia tomatoes.

150
00:08:11,630 --> 00:08:13,760
They are sweet and pop
in your mouth. I love it.

151
00:08:14,330 --> 00:08:16,630
Did your mother pack these for you?

152
00:08:17,100 --> 00:08:18,370
Does she pack them
like this every day?

153
00:08:18,770 --> 00:08:20,870
No. This is the first time.

154
00:08:22,970 --> 00:08:25,310
Are they tastier because
they are an improved variety?

155
00:08:26,240 --> 00:08:28,050
Well, I am not really sure.

156
00:08:29,280 --> 00:08:32,620
Stevia cherry tomatoes are not
an improved variety,

157
00:08:32,680 --> 00:08:34,690
they are processed
regular cherry tomatoes.

158
00:08:35,190 --> 00:08:36,190
How?

159
00:08:36,290 --> 00:08:38,660
They soak the tomatoes
in a natural sweetener solution...

160
00:08:38,720 --> 00:08:41,760
called stevia,
and then apply pressure...

161
00:08:41,830 --> 00:08:44,030
to infuse the sweetness
inside the skin.

162
00:08:44,900 --> 00:08:46,460
So the accurate term
classifies them...

163
00:08:46,630 --> 00:08:48,800
as processed fruit
and vegetable products.

164
00:08:50,740 --> 00:08:53,870
How do you know
such detailed information, Min Hee?

165
00:08:54,610 --> 00:08:58,540
My dad used to run
a fruit stand a few years ago.

166
00:08:59,010 --> 00:09:00,750
I see.

167
00:09:01,350 --> 00:09:02,980
Then what does he do now?

168
00:09:03,680 --> 00:09:04,680
Ms. Se Na.

169
00:09:06,380 --> 00:09:09,120
He has been in the intensive
care unit for four years.

170
00:09:11,820 --> 00:09:12,820
How did that happen?

171
00:09:14,060 --> 00:09:16,090
He was out on a delivery
on his motorcycle...

172
00:09:16,960 --> 00:09:18,100
and got hit by a bus.

173
00:09:19,500 --> 00:09:22,000
Da Mi.
Why are you only eating the banana,

174
00:09:22,070 --> 00:09:23,470
when there is expensive fruit
right here?

175
00:09:23,940 --> 00:09:26,540
- Open wide. Hurry up.
- Okay, I'll eat it.

176
00:09:30,340 --> 00:09:31,580
It is delicious.

177
00:09:34,610 --> 00:09:37,480
As expected, what my grandma said
is not wrong at all.

178
00:09:37,720 --> 00:09:40,320
My grandma always
used to say something.

179
00:09:41,120 --> 00:09:44,020
Consider every stranger
your teacher.

180
00:09:45,660 --> 00:09:48,830
Meeting like this is fate,
no, destiny,

181
00:09:48,990 --> 00:09:50,490
and you even gave me
this delicious fruit.

182
00:09:50,800 --> 00:09:52,930
I should repay you, right?

183
00:09:54,030 --> 00:09:58,700
Now, if you two ever
need my help in the future,

184
00:09:58,770 --> 00:10:00,200
please call me, Cha Se Na.

185
00:10:03,170 --> 00:10:04,180
(Grandma)

186
00:10:07,380 --> 00:10:08,380
This is delicious!

187
00:10:11,120 --> 00:10:15,320
- Where are you?
- I am... No, I am working.

188
00:10:15,520 --> 00:10:16,990
No matter where you are
or what you are doing,

189
00:10:17,220 --> 00:10:19,360
stop right now
and come back immediately.

190
00:10:19,660 --> 00:10:20,660
Why, what is wrong?

191
00:10:21,060 --> 00:10:22,660
You will see when you get here.

192
00:10:27,870 --> 00:10:29,200
I think I have to go.

193
00:10:38,210 --> 00:10:39,810
I wonder if she is at the store.

194
00:10:40,750 --> 00:10:41,750
Should I go again?

195
00:10:42,710 --> 00:10:43,710
Team Leader Cha.

196
00:10:44,650 --> 00:10:45,650
Assistant Manager Kang.

197
00:10:46,220 --> 00:10:49,050
I heard you went out of the office.
What did you go out for?

198
00:10:49,320 --> 00:10:50,320
I am sorry.

199
00:10:50,650 --> 00:10:52,560
I had to leave in a hurry
under CEO Jeon's orders,

200
00:10:52,620 --> 00:10:54,260
so I did not have time
to report to you separately.

201
00:10:55,160 --> 00:10:59,230
As you know, Team Leader Cha,
she had her shoe heel repaired...

202
00:10:59,360 --> 00:11:00,630
at the K Department Store
VIP lounge,

203
00:11:01,130 --> 00:11:02,570
and because that heel broke,

204
00:11:02,630 --> 00:11:05,500
the meeting with Summit Investment
was canceled.

205
00:11:07,340 --> 00:11:08,340
And so?

206
00:11:08,410 --> 00:11:10,670
I went to the store
on behalf of CEO Jeon...

207
00:11:10,740 --> 00:11:12,810
and filed a strong complaint.

208
00:11:14,710 --> 00:11:16,780
Does that mean
you met Manager Kang Da Mi?

209
00:11:16,950 --> 00:11:20,520
Oh my, you even remember...

210
00:11:20,620 --> 00:11:21,750
that employee's name,
Team Leader Cha.

211
00:11:22,620 --> 00:11:24,290
It is so ridiculous.

212
00:11:24,960 --> 00:11:26,960
I mean, even after causing
such a huge accident,

213
00:11:27,020 --> 00:11:28,360
her expression
did not change at all,

214
00:11:28,530 --> 00:11:29,890
and she acted so confidently,

215
00:11:30,230 --> 00:11:31,630
saying she would
follow the procedure.

216
00:11:32,700 --> 00:11:34,370
For a mere
department store employee,

217
00:11:34,430 --> 00:11:36,230
she was so shameless.

218
00:11:39,870 --> 00:11:41,010
Look here, Assistant Manager Kang.

219
00:11:41,570 --> 00:11:44,010
What exactly do you mean
by a mere department store employee?

220
00:11:45,440 --> 00:11:48,050
In your mind,
are department store employees...

221
00:11:49,050 --> 00:11:50,250
somehow beneath you?

222
00:11:51,420 --> 00:11:54,120
No, I mean...

223
00:11:57,050 --> 00:11:59,890
I am sorry, Team Leader Cha.
I misspoke.

224
00:12:00,360 --> 00:12:01,790
No job is beneath another.

225
00:12:07,330 --> 00:12:09,700
Who does not know that?

226
00:12:11,040 --> 00:12:13,470
But let us be honest,
we live in a world where it exists.

227
00:12:13,540 --> 00:12:14,570
Am I wrong?

228
00:12:16,240 --> 00:12:17,540
I am upset.

229
00:12:23,210 --> 00:12:24,420
I am sorry, Min Hee.

230
00:12:25,120 --> 00:12:28,190
On a day like today, I should be
drinking a beer with you.

231
00:12:30,750 --> 00:12:31,990
Do not worry too much.

232
00:12:32,060 --> 00:12:34,560
I explained the situation
to the higher-ups,

233
00:12:34,630 --> 00:12:35,730
so everything will be fine.

234
00:12:36,890 --> 00:12:38,960
Yes, thank you, Da Mi.

235
00:12:40,030 --> 00:12:43,230
You should hurry before they close.
You might have to run.

236
00:12:58,450 --> 00:13:01,520
(205,200 Dollars)

237
00:13:07,830 --> 00:13:10,860
(205,200 Dollars)

238
00:13:14,400 --> 00:13:16,800
I have been asking you
for nights on end,

239
00:13:16,870 --> 00:13:19,140
so why are you not
answering me, whoever's up there?

240
00:13:19,640 --> 00:13:20,700
Are you very busy?

241
00:13:21,340 --> 00:13:22,970
Did you go on a vacation
or something?

242
00:13:48,970 --> 00:13:50,000
Oh, man.

243
00:13:51,340 --> 00:13:53,140
At least I spilled it on the floor.

244
00:14:00,610 --> 00:14:02,680
Why does this keep bothering me?

245
00:14:05,720 --> 00:14:07,420
Should I just hand over the notebook
and be done with it?

246
00:14:20,030 --> 00:14:21,200
(Organza, Chiffon)

247
00:14:21,670 --> 00:14:23,670
(Keep the overall silhouette,
but reduce the frills' weight!)

248
00:14:23,970 --> 00:14:26,200
Was I too harsh?

249
00:14:28,470 --> 00:14:30,770
Take it easy, Head Designer.

250
00:14:31,780 --> 00:14:33,210
Did you have lunch?

251
00:14:33,740 --> 00:14:34,750
My gosh.

252
00:14:35,050 --> 00:14:38,020
You are making me feel pressured,
Team Leader Cha.

253
00:14:38,050 --> 00:14:40,280
Even worrying about my meals.
Hey, Do Yun.

254
00:14:40,350 --> 00:14:42,250
Hey, do not move. Do not move.

255
00:14:42,320 --> 00:14:43,590
It is slippery,
so just stand right there.

256
00:14:43,890 --> 00:14:45,590
We should call the cleaning lady.

257
00:14:46,060 --> 00:14:48,390
No, it is fine.
I can clean it up slowly later.

258
00:14:49,530 --> 00:14:50,530
What brings you by?

259
00:14:50,790 --> 00:14:52,560
Well, I just wanted to see
if you were slacking off...

260
00:14:52,630 --> 00:14:54,800
or working hard, so I stopped by.

261
00:14:55,300 --> 00:14:56,800
If you were sitting here
spacing out,

262
00:14:56,870 --> 00:14:57,870
I was going to scold you.

263
00:15:00,800 --> 00:15:02,210
How scary.

264
00:15:02,270 --> 00:15:04,840
Yes, understood, Team Leader Cha.
I will work hard.

265
00:15:07,210 --> 00:15:09,410
Do you happen to know
Dr. Ju's number?

266
00:15:09,950 --> 00:15:11,350
If you know it,
could you give it to me?

267
00:15:11,850 --> 00:15:15,490
You don't have his number, right?
Okay, I will send it right away.

268
00:15:15,690 --> 00:15:16,690
Get back to work.

269
00:15:17,050 --> 00:15:20,160
Mom has an important meeting
with an investment firm today,

270
00:15:20,220 --> 00:15:21,290
so I need to go see her.

271
00:15:22,460 --> 00:15:23,460
Hey, little brother.

272
00:15:24,260 --> 00:15:25,260
Yes?

273
00:15:29,430 --> 00:15:30,700
Hypothetically speaking.

274
00:15:31,100 --> 00:15:34,610
While I am working at the company,

275
00:15:34,670 --> 00:15:36,710
I might clash with CEO Jeon,
no, no...

276
00:15:37,040 --> 00:15:39,680
I might end up clashing with
your mother.

277
00:15:40,110 --> 00:15:43,280
If, by any chance, that happens,
would you...

278
00:15:44,920 --> 00:15:46,880
take your mother's side?

279
00:15:48,590 --> 00:15:50,690
Of course.

280
00:15:51,360 --> 00:15:53,460
At work, she is the person I serve,

281
00:15:53,660 --> 00:15:55,990
and at home,
she is the mom who raised me.

282
00:15:58,130 --> 00:15:59,300
Right, that is a great answer.

283
00:16:00,630 --> 00:16:01,630
Go get back to work.

284
00:16:01,970 --> 00:16:05,170
Wow, you are so anti-climactic.
Why ask something so obvious?

285
00:16:05,470 --> 00:16:06,470
I am leaving.

286
00:16:18,050 --> 00:16:19,350
Come on, Grandma.

287
00:16:20,050 --> 00:16:21,550
My only leverage...

288
00:16:21,620 --> 00:16:23,790
is being your granddaughter
and part of the Hwanggeum family,

289
00:16:24,290 --> 00:16:26,290
but if you tell me
I can never use that card,

290
00:16:26,520 --> 00:16:30,390
how am I supposed to collect
all of that massive debt?

291
00:16:30,890 --> 00:16:34,200
- That Kang Dae Chi is no easy mark.
- My gosh.

292
00:16:34,900 --> 00:16:35,900
Listen, kid.

293
00:16:36,200 --> 00:16:39,100
Living in this world
is not easy in itself.

294
00:16:39,570 --> 00:16:43,240
If you ever disobey me,

295
00:16:43,640 --> 00:16:46,810
forget about the investment funds.
You will be kicked out of my house.

296
00:16:46,880 --> 00:16:49,050
I mean, you raised me
like a fragile plant...

297
00:16:49,180 --> 00:16:50,410
in a greenhouse all my life,

298
00:16:50,480 --> 00:16:53,280
and now you are suddenly pushing me
off a cliff into the real world.

299
00:16:53,350 --> 00:16:59,320
- That is just too harsh.
- Get your facts straight.

300
00:16:59,320 --> 00:17:00,720
I am not the one who raised you...

301
00:17:00,720 --> 00:17:02,090
like a fragile plant
in a greenhouse.

302
00:17:02,460 --> 00:17:04,090
Your parents did that.

303
00:17:04,400 --> 00:17:08,970
Opening a tiny coffee shop
and growing the business...

304
00:17:09,170 --> 00:17:11,870
is no easy feat in today's world.

305
00:17:13,000 --> 00:17:17,810
I am going to test
your survival skills,

306
00:17:18,480 --> 00:17:19,480
so quit if you are upset.

307
00:17:20,210 --> 00:17:22,380
I have nothing to lose.

308
00:17:22,880 --> 00:17:27,680
Who said I was upset?
And my mouth is not crooked.

309
00:17:28,050 --> 00:17:29,420
I take after you, Grandma,
so my features...

310
00:17:29,490 --> 00:17:31,990
are perfectly and beautifully
placed right where they belong.

311
00:17:42,400 --> 00:17:46,100
Se Na may be a girl,
but she has grit.

312
00:17:46,840 --> 00:17:48,070
Do you not agree, Mrs. Anseong?

313
00:17:48,870 --> 00:17:49,940
Yes, ma'am.

314
00:17:50,470 --> 00:17:52,980
With a little polishing,
she will be quite something.

315
00:17:53,040 --> 00:17:54,040
You can go.

316
00:17:54,910 --> 00:17:56,980
She is probably out
in the living room right now,

317
00:17:57,250 --> 00:18:01,350
pouting her lips
and kicking her feet.

318
00:18:01,750 --> 00:18:03,590
Yes, please get some rest.

319
00:18:03,690 --> 00:18:05,790
You have been staring
at your laptop all morning.

320
00:18:20,200 --> 00:18:21,570
(Hwanggeum Capital Transitions
Outsourced Cleaning, Security,)

321
00:18:21,570 --> 00:18:22,740
(and Facility Management Staff
to Permanent Positions)

322
00:18:22,840 --> 00:18:23,840
What?

323
00:18:24,340 --> 00:18:26,940
Wow, I have never seen
such an idiot.

324
00:18:30,110 --> 00:18:32,880
I distributed the press release
just like you told me to,

325
00:18:33,380 --> 00:18:35,720
and now we have jumped
from third place...

326
00:18:35,790 --> 00:18:37,350
straight to second place
in trending topics.

327
00:18:38,060 --> 00:18:41,560
The way your brain works
is truly amazing.

328
00:18:42,330 --> 00:18:43,330
Thank you.

329
00:18:43,790 --> 00:18:46,560
Converting all the janitors,
guards, and managers...

330
00:18:46,630 --> 00:18:49,770
from temporary contractors
to full-time employees...

331
00:18:49,930 --> 00:18:52,070
cost your company a fortune,

332
00:18:52,270 --> 00:18:54,000
so we need to recover it
as quickly as possible.

333
00:18:55,010 --> 00:18:57,010
It's a story of noblesse oblige.

334
00:18:57,470 --> 00:19:00,140
It is only right
to promote you widely...

335
00:19:00,210 --> 00:19:02,610
as a good entrepreneur
contributing to society, right?

336
00:19:04,850 --> 00:19:08,390
But why did I not
think of that sooner?

337
00:19:09,420 --> 00:19:12,220
I really cannot live without you.

338
00:19:13,290 --> 00:19:15,190
(Mother)

339
00:19:15,260 --> 00:19:16,260
Honey.

340
00:19:16,430 --> 00:19:18,030
Mother must have seen
the article too.

341
00:19:18,360 --> 00:19:19,960
She is going to be thrilled.

342
00:19:20,930 --> 00:19:23,930
You did a great job.
Good luck with your meeting,

343
00:19:24,030 --> 00:19:26,840
and let's celebrate at home later.

344
00:19:27,340 --> 00:19:28,510
Okay, honey.

345
00:19:30,840 --> 00:19:33,410
(CEO Cha In Sung)

346
00:19:33,480 --> 00:19:34,610
Yes, Mother.

347
00:19:35,050 --> 00:19:36,750
You are calling because
you saw the article, right?

348
00:19:37,110 --> 00:19:39,420
You little punk!

349
00:19:39,480 --> 00:19:41,920
Step down from that position
right now!

350
00:19:43,520 --> 00:19:45,860
Excuse me? Mother,

351
00:19:46,290 --> 00:19:47,930
what did you just say?

352
00:19:49,430 --> 00:19:52,400
What kind of world
do you think we live in...

353
00:19:52,930 --> 00:19:54,830
to publish such
a patronizing article...

354
00:19:54,900 --> 00:19:58,000
and make such a fuss?

355
00:19:58,840 --> 00:20:02,370
As an executive, it is something
you should have done already.

356
00:20:03,040 --> 00:20:06,710
You acted only on my orders,
and you did it reluctantly,

357
00:20:06,910 --> 00:20:10,480
so how dare you lie to the public?

358
00:20:11,350 --> 00:20:13,420
Is that how I raised you?

359
00:20:14,150 --> 00:20:18,060
Mother.
While proceeding as you instructed,

360
00:20:18,160 --> 00:20:21,090
it is true that it became
a financial burden on the company.

361
00:20:21,630 --> 00:20:23,790
It is only beneficial for
the company's public relations,

362
00:20:23,860 --> 00:20:25,630
and it is not a bad thing, so why...

363
00:20:25,700 --> 00:20:26,700
Public relations?

364
00:20:27,200 --> 00:20:29,370
What a load of nonsense.

365
00:20:29,900 --> 00:20:32,670
You are fired as of this moment.

366
00:20:33,270 --> 00:20:36,410
- Step down.
- Mother.

367
00:20:37,940 --> 00:20:40,540
(CEO Cha In Sung)

368
00:20:40,610 --> 00:20:41,950
This is driving me crazy.

369
00:20:43,350 --> 00:20:45,280
Did I do this just for myself?

370
00:20:45,650 --> 00:20:47,520
I did it to save
the company's image.

371
00:20:51,990 --> 00:20:54,760
But am I really fired?

372
00:20:57,430 --> 00:20:58,430
Seriously.

373
00:20:58,560 --> 00:21:00,230
(Haedeul Bank)

374
00:21:05,670 --> 00:21:07,640
I apologize for the wait, ma'am.

375
00:21:08,340 --> 00:21:09,670
No, it is fine.

376
00:21:12,180 --> 00:21:14,680
This matures if you pay
for just half a year more,

377
00:21:15,210 --> 00:21:16,950
so I was a bit surprised
when you called.

378
00:21:23,550 --> 00:21:26,060
I prepared it as you requested.

379
00:21:26,420 --> 00:21:27,660
Yes, thank you.

380
00:21:27,720 --> 00:21:29,560
(Final Payout: 218,870 Dollars)

381
00:21:30,760 --> 00:21:33,700
By the way, do you remember...

382
00:21:33,760 --> 00:21:36,000
the tote bag you recommended?

383
00:21:36,730 --> 00:21:39,000
My mother absolutely loves it,

384
00:21:39,070 --> 00:21:41,440
and she has been showing it off
to the whole neighborhood.

385
00:21:41,670 --> 00:21:43,040
- Really?
- Yes.

386
00:21:43,110 --> 00:21:44,140
You mentioned gifting it...

387
00:21:44,170 --> 00:21:46,540
- when she turned 80.
- Yes.

388
00:21:46,910 --> 00:21:49,050
You have a great memory, Da Mi.

389
00:21:49,150 --> 00:21:52,720
- Remembering such small details.
- Of course I should remember.

390
00:21:52,920 --> 00:21:54,920
We have known each other
for years, Branch Manager.

391
00:21:56,620 --> 00:21:58,060
She takes that expensive bag
everywhere,

392
00:21:58,190 --> 00:22:01,990
even to the senior center
and the grocery store.

393
00:22:03,160 --> 00:22:05,330
When I bring it in
for repairs later,

394
00:22:05,400 --> 00:22:06,730
you will take good care
of it, right?

395
00:22:07,060 --> 00:22:09,430
Of course. Call me anytime.

396
00:22:11,130 --> 00:22:14,240
I will get going now.
I have somewhere to be.

397
00:22:16,170 --> 00:22:17,840
Da Mi.

398
00:22:18,540 --> 00:22:21,680
- Yes.
- I do not know what is going on,

399
00:22:22,110 --> 00:22:26,420
but since we have known each other
personally for a while now,

400
00:22:27,150 --> 00:22:28,490
I am a little worried.

401
00:22:30,550 --> 00:22:31,820
(Installment Savings
Early Cancellation Confirmation)

402
00:22:31,890 --> 00:22:32,890
I am just...

403
00:22:33,890 --> 00:22:36,390
doing what I have to do.

404
00:22:36,930 --> 00:22:38,100
Do not worry.

405
00:22:39,800 --> 00:22:42,000
I will be back soon
to open a new account.

406
00:22:42,400 --> 00:22:45,870
Then I will open the pension account
you recommended last time.

407
00:22:47,070 --> 00:22:50,170
And it will be strictly
for my own future.

408
00:22:51,270 --> 00:22:52,310
See you later.

409
00:22:55,480 --> 00:22:57,480
(Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

410
00:23:08,890 --> 00:23:12,730
What? Go see a gynecologist?

411
00:23:13,260 --> 00:23:16,230
Menopause? Unbelievable.

412
00:23:16,300 --> 00:23:18,700
I am still in my prime.

413
00:23:21,140 --> 00:23:23,340
Picking out shriveled jujubes.
Story of my life.

414
00:23:26,040 --> 00:23:28,510
I should go out and buy
some fresh jujubes to eat.

415
00:23:28,850 --> 00:23:32,520
I am never going to get old.
It is not fair.

416
00:23:33,380 --> 00:23:34,420
Darn it.

417
00:23:41,890 --> 00:23:43,890
(Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

418
00:23:50,570 --> 00:23:52,270
(Daeyang Bank)

419
00:23:54,500 --> 00:23:57,210
I should have told Da Mi
before closing the account.

420
00:24:01,710 --> 00:24:04,680
I wonder if Ri Ja
handled the dinner rush well.

421
00:24:05,380 --> 00:24:06,750
Mother is in bed, too.

422
00:24:06,820 --> 00:24:08,790
(Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

423
00:24:12,860 --> 00:24:13,860
Ms. Jo.

424
00:24:17,630 --> 00:24:18,730
Yes, Dr. Ju.

425
00:24:19,400 --> 00:24:22,000
- But I feel a little...
- Are you very dizzy?

426
00:24:23,000 --> 00:24:26,170
- Lean on me and try to stand up.
- Okay.

427
00:24:27,700 --> 00:24:29,510
My head suddenly started spinning,

428
00:24:30,210 --> 00:24:32,580
- and I lost all my strength...
- It is okay.

429
00:24:33,040 --> 00:24:35,050
Is your blood pressure
usually on the lower side?

430
00:24:38,050 --> 00:24:39,980
I have symptoms
of orthostatic hypotension...

431
00:24:42,190 --> 00:24:44,620
I stopped taking medication
a few years ago.

432
00:24:45,460 --> 00:24:46,890
It had gotten better.

433
00:24:47,190 --> 00:24:51,430
Let's go to my clinic first
and check your blood pressure.

434
00:24:54,000 --> 00:24:56,000
(Ju Kyung Ho Internal Medicine)

435
00:24:57,870 --> 00:24:59,970
(Ju Kyung Ho Internal Medicine)

436
00:25:00,040 --> 00:25:02,070
(Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

437
00:25:03,270 --> 00:25:04,910
Oh, my goodness.

438
00:25:05,940 --> 00:25:07,310
When did the beautiful Mi Mi...

439
00:25:08,210 --> 00:25:09,210
get so...

440
00:25:17,820 --> 00:25:18,820
Mi Mi.

441
00:25:19,790 --> 00:25:20,890
Mi Mi.

442
00:25:27,230 --> 00:25:28,470
My boss.

443
00:25:30,070 --> 00:25:31,870
(Nursing Assistant Park Ji Young)

444
00:25:31,940 --> 00:25:33,800
I am nothing but a sinner.

445
00:25:46,020 --> 00:25:49,790
This wretched life. Will dwelling...

446
00:25:50,790 --> 00:25:52,060
on it put food on the table?

447
00:25:52,890 --> 00:25:53,960
Will it bring in any money?

448
00:25:58,190 --> 00:26:00,500
I should head out to the restaurant.

449
00:26:00,500 --> 00:26:04,730
The children must be working
their fingers to the bone.

450
00:26:36,330 --> 00:26:37,330
It's open.

451
00:26:38,170 --> 00:26:39,270
It's the same as before.

452
00:26:53,420 --> 00:26:54,420
Mom.

453
00:26:55,050 --> 00:26:56,050
Mom.

454
00:26:57,290 --> 00:26:58,660
Is it just my imagination?

455
00:26:59,660 --> 00:27:00,860
It probably is,

456
00:27:01,760 --> 00:27:03,830
but it definitely smells
like Mom's embrace.

457
00:27:04,360 --> 00:27:05,630
It is exactly the same.

458
00:27:07,060 --> 00:27:08,130
Oh, right.

459
00:27:23,150 --> 00:27:24,150
Who...

460
00:27:24,450 --> 00:27:25,750
Who is this?

461
00:27:26,650 --> 00:27:27,780
Right.

462
00:27:28,520 --> 00:27:32,590
My eyes are still perfectly fine.
I am glad I caught you.

463
00:27:32,860 --> 00:27:34,320
You stand right there.

464
00:27:34,720 --> 00:27:37,490
No, you have the wrong person.

465
00:27:37,630 --> 00:27:40,160
I came to the wrong house, ma'am.

466
00:27:41,230 --> 00:27:44,730
If I let you slip away this time,
my name is not Choi Soon Deok.

467
00:27:44,800 --> 00:27:46,700
Our family is famous
for being relentless,

468
00:27:46,770 --> 00:27:48,570
and we have the pedigree
to prove it.

469
00:27:48,770 --> 00:27:50,870
Are you not going to stop? You punk.

470
00:27:57,950 --> 00:27:59,720
(Mission: Mompossible)

471
00:28:00,720 --> 00:28:02,320
That wretched punk.

472
00:28:03,050 --> 00:28:04,290
You know Kang Da Mi, right?

473
00:28:04,350 --> 00:28:05,660
Could you give me
her contact information?

474
00:28:05,720 --> 00:28:07,660
Are you in touch with Manager Kang?

475
00:28:08,360 --> 00:28:09,430
Mother,

476
00:28:09,830 --> 00:28:12,100
the children's mother must have
taken good care of you.

477
00:28:12,400 --> 00:28:14,060
You are still as beautiful as ever.

478
00:28:14,130 --> 00:28:16,400
Do not ever show your face
near our house again.

479
00:28:16,470 --> 00:28:17,470
Do you understand?

480
00:28:17,670 --> 00:28:19,670
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
